{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! Now I understand the data structure. I can see:\n1. Farmers markets data has state names and a farmers_markets column with counts\n2. Census data has NAME (state name) and POPESTIMATE2025 (2025 population)\n3. SUMLEV=40 filters to state-level data\n\nNow I need to create a build script that:\n1. Reads both sources\n2. Joins them on state name (farmers_markets.state_name == census.NAME)\n3. Filters census to state level (SUMLEV=40)\n4. Calculates totals and the ratio\n\nLet me create that script.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create a build script that joins both datasets and calculates the farmers markets per 100,000 residents metric:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01TFQLyvPv9z1Nq48BjUUQLq","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read both sources\nfm = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Filter census to state level (SUMLEV=40) and select relevant columns\ncensus_states = census.filter(census.SUMLEV == 40).select(\"NAME\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\")\n\n# Join on state name\njoined = fm.join(census_states, fm.state_name == census_states.NAME)\n\n# Calculate totals and per-capita rate\nexpr = joined.aggregate(\n    total_markets=fm.farmers_markets.sum(),\n    total_population=census_states.POPESTIMATE2025.sum()\n).mutate(\n    markets_per_100k=(joined.farmers_markets.sum() / census_states.POPESTIMATE2025.sum()) * 100000\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":697,"cacheRead":20859,"cacheWrite":3297,"totalTokens":24867,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0034850000000000003,"cacheRead":0.0020859000000000003,"cacheWrite":0.00412125,"total":0.00970615},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":152},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914546471,"responseId":"msg_011Ce77TBYc3ZBRh7vcHJ6uL","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01TFQLyvPv9z1Nq48BjUUQLq","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1201 bytes to .xorq/scripts/markets_per_capita.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914555001}]}
